WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.600
So anyway, in conclusion, the best thing Kevin&nbsp;
Feige did was making Cowboys and Aliens starring&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:14.160
Jon Favreau. I'm here with Tom and Nina to ask the&nbsp;
question, what are the best and worst decisions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:17.680
Kevin Feige has made with the MCU.&nbsp;
Nina, why don't you start us off?

00:00:18.640 --> 00:00:24.480
Thanks, Brian. So worst is tough because as&nbsp;
you said, most of these movies are pretty good.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:30.000
They've performed really spectacularly well at&nbsp;
the box office. They're critically ... For the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.880
most part, I mean, Avengers: Infinity War and&nbsp;
Endgame did very well with critics. Many of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:39.920
smaller ones have as well. So I think worst is,&nbsp;
is tough. And it's very relative when it comes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:43.760
to Kevin Feige running the MCU, because&nbsp;
he's done a really good job as somebody-

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:45.840
It's hard to find the bad&nbsp;
stuff amongst so much good.

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:50.400
But something that concerns me. And I'll&nbsp;
admit that when I was doing research for this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:53.600
I stumbled across a piece written&nbsp;
by Emily VanDerWerff, who is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:57.680
I believe the critic at large at&nbsp;
Fox. And she made a good point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.680 --> 00:01:02.720
where she was like, "The MCU is the&nbsp;
most television-esque thing in film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:07.600
right now," in that sure, you can watch the&nbsp;
movies by themselves, but they're really episodic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:13.440
And if you watch Captain America: Winter Soldier&nbsp;
without having seen the first Captain America,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:18.560
you don't really understand why he is really&nbsp;
anxious about government oversight. You don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:22.080
really get like the smaller kind of character&nbsp;
beats if you don't watch the entire thing.

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:29.120
And I think that, that level of interconnectedness&nbsp;
can get really tricky because then you start,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:32.800
especially with so many movies, I think that&nbsp;
a casual viewer might start to feel alienated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:37.760
by the entire thing. And I think that, that&nbsp;
concerns me going forward. I mean, an example is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:42.080
during quarantine, I live near my parents, we&nbsp;
watched a lot of movies together. I couldn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:45.600
have shown them Infinity War Endgame. They would&nbsp;
have been like, "Who were any of these people?"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:48.720
Because they don't watch Marvel movies. But&nbsp;
I can show them Black Panther because it is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:53.440
a complete standalone. And you can understand&nbsp;
that movie really, really well without ... Even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:56.640
though Klaue is in other movies, you&nbsp;
don't need to know who he is beforehand.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:59.360
You don't really need to&nbsp;
know who he is during either.

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:03.600
No. And even if you haven't seen Captain America:&nbsp;
Civil war and the introduction of T'Challah,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:07.040
you don't really need that either. You&nbsp;
just know when this movie opens that his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:12.560
father has passed away. So I think the&nbsp;
interconnectedness is a great strength,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:15.040
but it could be a weakness, in&nbsp;
that I think it could alienate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:20.800
more casual viewers who don't want to watch&nbsp;
20-plus movies to understand what's going on.

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:25.600
